                "reviews": [
                    {
                        "recommendationid": "238346511",
                        "author": {
                            "steamid": "76561198980678735",
                            "num_reviews": 19,
                            "playtime_forever": 61,
                            "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0,
                            "playtime_at_review": 61,
                            "last_played": 1792720776
                        },
                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "[h3] A Masterpiece of Its Time, Not For Casual Players Today 4/10 [/h3]\n\nI bought the collector bundle on sale because I loved the ones on the Xbox 360 and wanted to relive those memories through seeing the originals since I never had the chance to play them. I knew it would be a more difficult game and have a lot of differences. The price is very fair and if you just want to have the entire set that's fine. However, personally I can't recommend this title to modern or casual players today for a few reasons.\n\nThe UI is incredibly clunky, the mechanics are frustratingly all over the place, and overall has aged poorly. Combat difficulty spikes randomly and bugs appear occasionally. That being said, I understand this came out in 1994 and was a phenomenal gem with high praises and awards. I can definitely see why. From customizing your units, ships, bases, and traveling across the world. It is clear why so many fans love this and have a dedicated community.\n\nIf you enjoy the history of X-COM or want a retro experience pick it up, but if you don't want to dedicate the time into learning how the gameplay and tactics work I wouldn't try to attempt it if I'm being honest.",
